#                       super-block for Q4_K, six for Q5_K, seven for Q6_K) instead of a dword
#                       gather per lane per dword. Rows past the matrix read as zeros and are
#                       dropped where they always were. Otherwise 0028's staged path, unchanged.
#   kquant_utils.cl     The three decodes from a super-block already in registers (kq_dec_*_w),
#                       the same arithmetic as the pointer forms.
#   fully_connected_kernel_kquant.cpp   KQ_2D from the architecture, the type, the row pitch (a
#                       multiple of 16 bytes) and the input's layout (pitches equal to the
#                       logical dims on every axis, no first-element offset: the block is
#                       addressed from the buffer's start at a pitch of K); ARCINT_KQ_2D=0
#                       forces the staged path for measurement. The row tile is 64 on Xe2, 32 on
#                       Xe-HPG, and the tiled kernel alone is compiled in the 256-register mode
#                       (-cl-intel-256-GRF-per-thread, its own batch); the decode kernel stays at
#                       128, where it measured better (DESIGN 7.0.2bd).
#   fully_connected_gpu_test.cpp   The timing test's activations and weights in device memory
#                       (allocate_memory(layout) is the lockable host allocation: every tiled
#                       figure the test gave before this patch timed the bus), valid scales in
#                       its rows, and the served row count (856) among its shapes.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-07 (correctness 21/21 on both cards at the shipped configuration), the timing
# test in device memory, us per launch, 0028 -> 0029:
